<title>ITALY: Italy parlt suspends debate, awaits Prodi.</title>
<headline>Italy parlt suspends debate, awaits Prodi.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's Chamber of Deputies (lower house) suspended a debate on the 1997 budget briefly on Thursday ahead of the arrival of Prime Minister Romano Prodi.</p>
<p>The opposition centre-right Freedom Alliance, which is blocking the budget, has called on Prodi to explain why he has rejected their request to strip from the budget package special law-making powers.</p>
<p>Prodi's 1997 budget aims to slash next year's deficit by 62.5 trillion lire.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 678 2501</p>
</text>
